WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.285
{\an8}[announcer]
<i>The winner of</i> I Am Boxer <i>will receive</i>

2
00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:19.920
{\an8}<i>a grand prize of 300 million won</i>

3
00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:23.190
{\an8}<i>and a top-of-the-line flagship SUV.</i>

4
00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.533
[exhaling]

5
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.639
Hi, I'm Don Lee,
actor and local gym owner,

6
00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.409
and the Master of <i>I Am Boxer</i>.

7
00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.946
For years, I've envisioned this stage.

8
00:00:47.748 --> 00:00:51.818
For boxers brimming with incredible talent
but who never got their chance to shine.

9
00:00:52.853 --> 00:00:54.688
[boxer 1]
I'll put my heart and soul into this.

10
00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:57.024
[boxer 2]
Either I go down or my opponent does.

11
00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.926
[boxer 3]
It all comes down to who wants it more.

12
00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:03.163
I wanted to give them
the biggest stage of their lives.

13
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:07.100
[bell rings]

14
00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.937
[announcer] <i>This is where Korean fighters
will come to challenge themselves.</i>

15
00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.738
- [contestant 1] What?
- [contestant 2] What the heck?

16
00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.273
- This is it!
- [referee, in English] Box!

17
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.142
- Box.
- [in Korean] Go, go!

18
00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.276
- That's it!
- You got it!

19
00:01:16.343 --> 00:01:18.779
Background, age, weight class...

20
00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.814
None of it matters here.

21
00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.584
[Lee]
<i>Number one fighter among celebrities.</i>

22
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.018
[crowd cheering]

23
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.120
[onlooker] That's it! You're doing great!

24
00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.488
[boxer 1] Shut your mouth, bastard.

25
00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.223
[boxer 2] <i>I thought you can
knock me out?</i> [chuckles]

26
00:01:30.691 --> 00:01:31.692
[commentator] He's on a roll.

27
00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.727
[onlooker]
Yes, that's it! Down, down, down!

28
00:01:33.794 --> 00:01:35.495
<i>Losing's gonna freaking suck, man!</i>

29
00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.564
[Lee] At the end of it all,

30
00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.033
only one will survive

31
00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.603
and claim the title of champion.

32
00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.306
[commentator]
This fighter has returned to the ring.

33
00:01:46.373 --> 00:01:47.874
[Lee] An extreme journey of survival.

34
00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:51.612
This is where you must pour
your mind, body, and soul.

35
00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:55.449
I've been thinking hard about
whether I should quit.

36
00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.918
Boxing still excites me
just as much as ever. [cries]

37
00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.587
- [Lee] Tonight...
- [shouts]

38
00:02:00.654 --> 00:02:03.724
...witness the toughest boxers
battle it out in the most intense fights.

39
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:04.858
<i>I Am Boxer</i>

40
00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:07.527
starts right now.

41
00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:09.830
[exhaling]

42
00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:37.024
Whoa, that's a lot of names. This is huge.

43
00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:42.262
Hello, I'm Kuk Seungjun
from the Hwasun County boxing team.

44
00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:44.665
I've been boxing for 13 years.

45
00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:47.901
I was a gold medalist at the 100th

46
00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:50.737
and 105th Korean National Sports Festival.

47
00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.413
Seeing those boxing trunks
with my name on them

48
00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.381
really got me pumped.

49
00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.485
There's no turning back now.
I have to win this.

50
00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:13.627
There's plenty competition.

51
00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.441
<i>Hello, I'm Kwon Ohgon,
former Korean champion</i>

52
00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.644
in both the lightweight
and super lightweight divisions.

53
00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:32.713
- [commentator 1] He's going in...
- [commentator 2] Nice one!

54
00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.949
[Kwon] I guess you could say
I'm a bit well-known in the boxing world.

55
00:03:36.016 --> 00:03:37.551
[commentator] Oh! He's down!

56
00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:42.122
[Kwon] I'm ready to take on anyone,
so feel free to step right up.

57
00:03:42.823 --> 00:03:45.292
- Damn.
- Whoa, it's huge in here.

58
00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.062
[Seol laughs]

59
00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:54.835
Hello, I'm Seol Yeongho,
winner of a martial arts survival show.

60
00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.303
Can I be honest here?

61
00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.904
It's time to clean house.

62
00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:01.341
Every group calls itself a federation,
and everyone claims they're a champion.

63
00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:03.777
I've sparred with these
so-called pro boxers,

64
00:04:03.844 --> 00:04:06.346
and a lot of them were
worse than MMA amateurs.

65
00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.483
Wow, that belt looks killer.

66
00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:23.764
[Kwon] I really didn't like him.

67
00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.832
Ever wear a belt
when you were still in the game?

68
00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.501
Of course I did.

69
00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.870
- I have yet to wear one.
- This one looks nicer.

70
00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.304
[both laughing]

71
00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.874
Ooh. Any familiar names?

72
00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:38.545
[Seol] Oh! We've got soldiers here too?

73
00:04:39.179 --> 00:04:41.114
- You guys from KAFAC?
- Yes, that's right.

74
00:04:41.181 --> 00:04:42.616
So you guys are all boxers?

75
00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:43.850
- Yes.
- Yes, that's right.

76
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:45.252
We've even got KAFAC guys here.

77
00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:47.721
- Private first class?
- [soldiers laughing]

78
00:04:47.788 --> 00:04:49.156
Still got a long way to go.

79
00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.391
[Seol]
I thought they all looked pretty soft.

80
00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:54.728
- Hey, look. A camera.
- Wait, is it rolling now?

81
00:04:57.264 --> 00:04:58.965
Oh!

82
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:01.034
Isn't that Yoon Hyeongbin?

83
00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.738
Wow, this place is massive. Wow.

84
00:05:04.805 --> 00:05:07.274
And the guy next to him
used to be an MMA fighter.

85
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.475
{\an8}[soldier 2] Wait, seriously?

86
00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:11.244
{\an8}[soldier 3] Well, we've got
some ROAD FC fighters too.

87
00:05:11.812 --> 00:05:13.079
Hey, look at that.

88
00:05:13.914 --> 00:05:15.549
[contestants murmuring]

89
00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.351
Wow, this is insane.

90
00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:21.021
Huh? What the hell?

91
00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.455
Oh!

92
00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.024
This is nuts, for real.

93
00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.692
Hello, sir.

94
00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:27.427
- Oh, hi.
- [contestants exclaiming, laughing]

95
00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:28.595
Good to see you.

96
00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.498
- Damn, this is no joke.
- This is crazy.

97
00:05:31.565 --> 00:05:33.133
- I'm such a fan.
- Thank you.

98
00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.669
- Go easy on us.
- Well, I'll do my best to win.

99
00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.070
Could I get a handshake?

100
00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:38.572
- Of course.
- Thank you.

101
00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.040
Man...

102
00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:43.610
He didn't even look human,
more like a walking fridge.

103
00:05:43.677 --> 00:05:46.413
What are you doing here? I mean...

104
00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.481
This isn't fair to the rest of us.

105
00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:52.752
Hello, I've been in combat sports
for about 20 years now.

106
00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:56.356
I've won championship titles
in seven different competitions.

107
00:05:57.023 --> 00:06:01.127
I'm on the heavier side
of the heavyweight division.

108
00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:05.165
I've got the kind of power
you don't usually see around here.

109
00:06:05.232 --> 00:06:07.467
- [commentators shouting, exclaiming]
- Knee kick!

110
00:06:08.235 --> 00:06:10.370
Myung Hyunman takes a fiery victory!

111
00:06:10.437 --> 00:06:13.840
I want to prove
that I'm the best in this country.

112
00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.076
I should've gotten life insurance.
[chuckles]

113
00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.411
You'll be in trouble
if you don't have coverage.

114
00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:21.948
- Wow.
- Well, he's good-looking.

115
00:06:22.015 --> 00:06:23.483
Wow.

116
00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:27.020
You'd never guess they're fighters
just by looking at their faces.

117
00:06:27.087 --> 00:06:28.788
Everyone is so good-looking.

118
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.858
- Wow.
- This is crazy.

119
00:06:31.925 --> 00:06:33.126
Wow.

120
00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.761
Whoa.

121
00:06:34.828 --> 00:06:36.162
He looks like a celebrity.

122
00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.397
Wow.

123
00:06:37.464 --> 00:06:38.999
Oh, it's Yuk Junseo.

124
00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.334
Hello, I'm Yuk Junseo.

125
00:06:42.202 --> 00:06:44.938
I'm an artist
and a television personality.

126
00:06:45.005 --> 00:06:50.911
Currently, I do weight training, running,
and boxing, all in one day.

127
00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:53.413
I'm always pretty much fired up.

128
00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.181
I'm always hungry for more.

129
00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.818
My ultimate goal is to win. [laughs]

130
00:06:59.586 --> 00:07:01.755
Confidence has never been an issue for me.

131
00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.657
If anything, I've got an excess of it.

132
00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:07.093
[contestant shouting]

133
00:07:10.397 --> 00:07:11.865
- [shouts]
- Whoa.

134
00:07:11.932 --> 00:07:14.301
Wow, he's huge.

135
00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.469
- Wow.
- He's in high school?

136
00:07:17.504 --> 00:07:18.905
- You're a high school senior?
- Yes.

137
00:07:18.972 --> 00:07:20.473
- A high school senior?
- Yes.

138
00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:22.108
Wow, he's super tall.

139
00:07:22.709 --> 00:07:23.710
This is intense.

140
00:07:23.777 --> 00:07:26.146
He's just squinting
because his eyesight is bad, right?

141
00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.883
- Wow.
- Nice to meet you all.

142
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.519
We've got all the top heavyweights
in Korea here.

143
00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:36.356
- Even Master Dduk is here.
- Karate, right?

144
00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.391
Oh, they're Muay Thai fighters?

145
00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:40.360
- What sport do you do?
- Kickboxing.

146
00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:42.529
I was a volleyball player.

147
00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:43.797
Volleyball? I see.

148
00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.633
[contestants exclaiming, applauding]

149
00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.868
{\an8}Wow, they've got an incredible physique.

150
00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:51.137
{\an8}They must be bodybuilders.

151
00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:52.205
{\an8}Hello there.

152
00:07:56.376 --> 00:07:57.377
Wow.

153
00:07:57.444 --> 00:08:00.547
[contestants exclaiming, applauding]

154
00:08:02.382 --> 00:08:03.550
It's Julien Kang.

155
00:08:05.819 --> 00:08:08.021
It's Julien. Now that's a total celebrity.

156
00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.290
He's got a crazy physique.

157
00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:12.225
Seriously, man.

158
00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:15.829
{\an8}He's number one fighter among celebrities.

159
00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.132
Julien Kang, the guy's built like a tank.

160
00:08:19.199 --> 00:08:21.301
He's famous for his fighting background.

161
00:08:21.368 --> 00:08:23.803
Search his name,
and you'll see "pro fighter" every time.

162
00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.073
{\an8}He's always been ranked top three
when it comes to fighting.

163
00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.211
- Hello.
- He's built differently.

164
00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:33.113
- Hello. Hi.
- I'm a big fan.

165
00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.115
He's like Captain America.

166
00:08:35.749 --> 00:08:37.384
Wow, this place is packed.

167
00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:41.221
[Kang] We've got
a lot of strong guys here.

168
00:08:44.858 --> 00:08:46.826
- Damn, the lineup's crazy.
- [applause]

169
00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:48.561
Well, damn it.

170
00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:50.363
I might as well go home now.

171
00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.500
- Game over.
- Game over.

172
00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:55.435
Well, if it isn't
the Korean national champion.

173
00:08:55.502 --> 00:08:57.537
Here comes another beast.

174
00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.774
Oh, come on. This is downright unfair.

175
00:09:02.342 --> 00:09:04.277
Is that Jung Dawoon?

176
00:09:04.344 --> 00:09:05.879
[cheering, applause continues]

177
00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.580
Time to go home. [laughs]

178
00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.550
Hello there. Oh, hey! [chuckles]

179
00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:14.921
I didn't expect
a fighter like him to show up.

180
00:09:14.988 --> 00:09:18.291
He's from
the world's top MMA organization.

181
00:09:18.825 --> 00:09:21.761
That instantly raises the bar
for this show.

182
00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:26.800
I'm a middleweight
who's fought on the world stage.

183
00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:31.471
When you step into my ring,
you'd better be ready to give it your all.

184
00:09:31.538 --> 00:09:33.440
[applause continues]

185
00:09:34.774 --> 00:09:38.178
- He started out as a boxer, though.
- That's why he's good at close combat.

186
00:09:38.845 --> 00:09:41.281
Jung Dawoon without a weight cut
sounds like a nightmare.

187
00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.683
Should've just stuck to selling
soy-marinated crabs.

188
00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.185
- [contestant laughing]
- Fucking hell.

189
00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:47.253
- [applause continues]
- Oh!

190
00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.055
[contestants exclaiming]

191
00:09:49.122 --> 00:09:50.824
We have two champions?

192
00:09:51.491 --> 00:09:53.493
Are they boxing champions?

193
00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.595
That's Kim Taesun.

194
00:09:55.662 --> 00:09:57.797
- Super featherweight.
- Oh, super featherweight?

195
00:09:57.864 --> 00:09:59.866
Wait, isn't he real famous?

196
00:09:59.933 --> 00:10:02.102
Yes, that's Minuk. He's formidable.

197
00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:04.504
Snyper Kim. He's the world-ranked.

198
00:10:04.571 --> 00:10:05.972
He's the real deal in boxing.

199
00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.409
Hello, I'm Kim Minuk,

200
00:10:09.476 --> 00:10:12.679
a former national team athlete
and OPBF champion.

201
00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:16.382
Most pro and amateur boxers
have probably heard of me.

202
00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:20.320
I'll show you what Kim Minuk is made of.
Just wait and see.

203
00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.623
There are already so many big names here.

204
00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.792
This is amazing. Everyone here is no joke.

205
00:10:26.593 --> 00:10:29.963
We have top-level fighters
from all over the country.

206
00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:32.398
This won't be easy at all.

207
00:10:33.066 --> 00:10:36.436
See? The main contenders are already set.

208
00:10:37.036 --> 00:10:38.404
- The latecomers?
- Yeah.

209
00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.141
Wait a sec.

210
00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:43.710
Wait, "Kim Donghoe"?
Looks like everyone's here.

211
00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:45.845
- Kim Donghoe's coming.
- Wow.

212
00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.848
Hear that? "Kim Donghoe."

213
00:10:48.915 --> 00:10:51.484
- He's won 13 straight national titles.
- Yeah, I know.

214
00:10:51.551 --> 00:10:52.986
- He's coming?
- Yeah.

215
00:10:56.022 --> 00:10:57.490
Wow.

216
00:10:57.557 --> 00:10:59.559
I got chills just now.

217
00:10:59.626 --> 00:11:01.294
I think we're fucked.

218
00:11:01.361 --> 00:11:03.229
[contestants exclaiming, applauding]

219
00:11:03.296 --> 00:11:05.798
Wow.

220
00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:08.168
Kim Donghoe and Kim Taekmin? For real?

221
00:11:08.902 --> 00:11:10.470
- Hello there.
- Hello.

222
00:11:10.537 --> 00:11:11.538
Oh, man.

223
00:11:12.906 --> 00:11:15.141
There's our legend. The Ghost.

224
00:11:16.109 --> 00:11:18.178
No one in this room can match him.

225
00:11:18.978 --> 00:11:20.079
There's our champion.

226
00:11:21.014 --> 00:11:23.349
- The current top two in boxing, right?
- Yeah.

227
00:11:23.816 --> 00:11:24.851
Is that you, Sungmin?

228
00:11:24.918 --> 00:11:26.619
{\an8}Why are you both here? [laughs]

229
00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.388
Just one of you would've been plenty.

230
00:11:29.289 --> 00:11:31.324
- This is wild.
- Kim Taekmin is a bit much, man.

231
00:11:32.158 --> 00:11:35.195
I've been keeping an eye on Kim Taekmin
for a while now.

232
00:11:35.261 --> 00:11:36.796
He's my role model.

233
00:11:36.863 --> 00:11:39.866
I've never even thought about losing
no matter who I face.

234
00:11:40.934 --> 00:11:42.335
Kim Donghoe.

235
00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:44.571
He's won the National Sports Festival...

236
00:11:44.637 --> 00:11:46.306
He's won it 13 years in a row.

237
00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:48.208
He's going for his 14th win now.

238
00:11:48.675 --> 00:11:52.011
Can anyone in Korea beat him?
I highly doubt it.

239
00:11:52.078 --> 00:11:53.446
They think they've landed a hit,

240
00:11:53.513 --> 00:11:55.982
but I've already slipped away
like a ghost, they say.

241
00:11:56.049 --> 00:12:00.320
If we're talking pure boxing,
I think I'm practically untouchable.

242
00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:02.422
I'm confident I'll win this thing.

243
00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:05.558
But what if some amateur beats him?
Then that's it for him, right?

244
00:12:05.625 --> 00:12:07.260
- But that's not happening.
- Exactly.

245
00:12:07.327 --> 00:12:08.328
That's never happening.

246
00:12:14.167 --> 00:12:16.569
How many are we, a hundred?

247
00:12:16.636 --> 00:12:17.804
Everyone's here, right?

248
00:12:19.439 --> 00:12:20.773
One person's still missing.

249
00:12:22.642 --> 00:12:24.944
- The actor?
- I think so.

250
00:12:25.011 --> 00:12:26.312
I'm a fan.

251
00:12:26.379 --> 00:12:28.915
- He's not here yet?
- Guess he's coming last.

252
00:12:32.885 --> 00:12:34.687
- [contestants exclaiming, applauding]
- There he is.

253
00:12:34.754 --> 00:12:36.689
The perfect finisher for this lineup.

254
00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:38.391
Seriously, Jang Hyuk is here?

255
00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:40.460
- No way.
- It's Jang Hyuk.

256
00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:43.263
I wasn't sure it was him,
but it really is.

257
00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:44.397
It's Jang Hyuk.

258
00:12:45.131 --> 00:12:46.232
Oh!

259
00:12:46.299 --> 00:12:48.701
Hello, I'm Jang Hyuk, an actor.

260
00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:49.902
Thank you for having me.

261
00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:55.375
[Jang] Working on a film project
always took a toll on me.

262
00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:57.410
Then one day,
I happened to walk into a boxing gym.

263
00:12:57.477 --> 00:13:01.180
I felt recharged after a boxing session.

264
00:13:01.247 --> 00:13:03.216
That's what kept me going.

265
00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:06.352
[announcer] Jang Hyuk,
you've passed the pro boxing test!

266
00:13:06.419 --> 00:13:09.055
[Jang] I wanted to see for myself

267
00:13:09.122 --> 00:13:11.858
how far I could go in this thing.

268
00:13:13.026 --> 00:13:16.029
[announcer] <i>All contestants have arrived.</i>

269
00:13:16.696 --> 00:13:19.666
<i>The blockbuster boxing survival show,</i>

270
00:13:19.732 --> 00:13:21.367
I Am Boxer...

271
00:13:25.438 --> 00:13:28.641
<i>starts right now.</i>

272
00:13:30.977 --> 00:13:33.079
I thought, "So this is it. It's begun."

273
00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:37.216
There's no turning back now.
From here on out, I have to go all in.

274
00:13:37.784 --> 00:13:40.053
[Kim Donghoe]
It doesn't matter who I'm up against.

275
00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.422
Either I go down or my opponent does.

276
00:13:43.356 --> 00:13:44.757
I'm taking first place.

277
00:13:44.824 --> 00:13:45.758
The victory is mine.

278
00:13:45.825 --> 00:13:49.862
I'll fight with everything I've got
till my opponent's on the canvas.

279
00:14:03.176 --> 00:14:04.210
This is intense. I'm nervous.

280
00:14:04.277 --> 00:14:06.879
- [contestants chattering]
- It's opening.

281
00:14:08.181 --> 00:14:10.016
[contestants exclaiming]

282
00:14:10.083 --> 00:14:11.084
What the heck?

283
00:14:11.718 --> 00:14:13.386
- No way.
- [in English] Oh, my God.

284
00:14:13.453 --> 00:14:15.321
[in Korean] Wow, this is enormous.

285
00:14:15.388 --> 00:14:17.123
God, this is freaking insane.

286
00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.092
Wow, this is sick.

287
00:14:20.226 --> 00:14:21.427
[in English] What the hell is this?

288
00:14:21.494 --> 00:14:23.529
[in Korean]
This is blockbuster-level, all right.

289
00:14:23.596 --> 00:14:25.231
This is massive.

290
00:14:27.367 --> 00:14:28.534
That's a killer concept.

291
00:14:28.601 --> 00:14:31.838
I didn't think a set could be this big.

292
00:14:32.405 --> 00:14:33.906
This is no joke. It's insane.

293
00:14:33.973 --> 00:14:36.142
Looks like it'd be fun to fight in here.

294
00:14:36.209 --> 00:14:38.845
My blood was pumping,
and I wanted to get fighting.

295
00:14:39.812 --> 00:14:40.947
What now?

296
00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:42.515
What are we doing here?

297
00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:45.151
I was super curious.

298
00:14:45.218 --> 00:14:47.420
It's even scarier
because there's nothing here.

299
00:14:49.055 --> 00:14:50.790
Why isn't there anything here?

300
00:14:50.857 --> 00:14:52.492
Are we supposed to fight without a ring?

301
00:14:52.558 --> 00:14:54.794
- Just like <i>Fight Club</i>, right?
- Yeah.

302
00:14:54.861 --> 00:14:57.096
What now? What's happening now?

303
00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:00.933
Feels like something might be
behind this thing.

304
00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.503
Do we fight the moment that door opens?

305
00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.671
- Kind of feels like it.
- Oh.

306
00:15:06.506 --> 00:15:08.007
No, there must be something in there.

307
00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:10.410
- A ring, maybe?
- Yeah, look over there.

308
00:15:10.476 --> 00:15:13.413
- That's where the cameras are set up.
- Oh, right.

309
00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.082
"Open sesame." You know what that means?

310
00:15:16.149 --> 00:15:17.550
When you say, "Open sesame,"

311
00:15:18.117 --> 00:15:20.453
- the door opens.
- Oh, right. [chuckles]

312
00:15:22.321 --> 00:15:24.323
Whoa, it's opening up.

313
00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:26.092
- [contestants exclaiming]
- Oh, what's that?

314
00:15:26.159 --> 00:15:27.560
- I was right.
- For real?

315
00:15:28.127 --> 00:15:30.296
- Wow, no way.
- This is insane.

316
00:15:31.964 --> 00:15:32.999
Wait, for real?

317
00:15:33.065 --> 00:15:35.501
- They actually put rings in there.
- [laughing]

318
00:15:35.568 --> 00:15:36.702
Nine rings? Really?

319
00:15:37.203 --> 00:15:38.805
Wow, they really put rings in there!

320
00:15:38.871 --> 00:15:41.441
Wait, what? We were right about that?

321
00:15:41.507 --> 00:15:44.076
- Are you serious?
- There's a ring in each space.

322
00:15:44.143 --> 00:15:45.845
Holy crap.

323
00:15:45.912 --> 00:15:47.046
Couldn't have imagined this.

324
00:15:47.113 --> 00:15:48.381
It's like a fight factory.

325
00:15:48.848 --> 00:15:50.116
A boxing factory.

326
00:15:50.183 --> 00:15:51.684
We're already going one-on-one?

327
00:15:51.751 --> 00:15:53.519
Wow, this is insane.

328
00:15:53.586 --> 00:15:55.354
There were nine rings.

329
00:15:55.421 --> 00:15:57.757
Wow, I never saw that coming.

330
00:15:58.391 --> 00:16:01.527
- So we're all having a match.
- Guess we're sparring today.

331
00:16:01.994 --> 00:16:03.629
Why is the middle one still closed?

332
00:16:03.696 --> 00:16:05.598
What's up with that one? Is it jammed?

333
00:16:05.665 --> 00:16:07.800
Feels like there's something big in there.

334
00:16:07.867 --> 00:16:09.569
Could it be...

335
00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:12.071
- Is Don Lee in there? No way.
- Could it be...

336
00:16:13.673 --> 00:16:15.441
Could it be... No way!

337
00:16:15.508 --> 00:16:17.910
- Oh! Oh!
- [contestants exclaiming]

338
00:16:17.977 --> 00:16:19.612
Whoa!

339
00:16:19.679 --> 00:16:21.914
The moment of truth!

340
00:16:22.815 --> 00:16:24.350
The moment of truth is here!

341
00:16:24.417 --> 00:16:27.353
[contestants exclaiming, cheering]

342
00:16:30.323 --> 00:16:33.493
Man, no way. I've got goose bumps.

343
00:16:44.637 --> 00:16:48.007
[cheering, exclaiming, applauding]

344
00:16:55.414 --> 00:16:57.984
- He looks awesome!
- He's huge.

345
00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.552
It felt like I was watching a movie.

346
00:16:59.619 --> 00:17:00.620
He was massive

347
00:17:01.287 --> 00:17:02.788
and really charismatic.

348
00:17:02.855 --> 00:17:04.190
I couldn't believe my eyes.

349
00:17:04.257 --> 00:17:07.660
He's like the Hulk
when he's about to burst out of his suit.

350
00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:09.829
That's the exact impression I got.

351
00:17:09.896 --> 00:17:12.164
He totally looked like
the boss of a fighting promotion.

352
00:17:12.231 --> 00:17:14.500
Like the chairman.

353
00:17:14.567 --> 00:17:15.735
Mavely!

354
00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:17.937
[cheering]

355
00:17:18.004 --> 00:17:20.039
Do I fight him if I make it to the finals?

356
00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.275
Is he going to fight us up there?

357
00:17:23.543 --> 00:17:25.878
[contestants exclaiming]

358
00:17:32.151 --> 00:17:33.152
This is insane.

359
00:17:38.024 --> 00:17:39.025
Hello.

360
00:17:39.091 --> 00:17:41.160
- Hello!
- Hello!

361
00:17:42.028 --> 00:17:47.333
I'm Don Lee, your local boxing gym owner,
and the Master of <i>I Am Boxer</i>.

362
00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.569
[contestants cheering]

363
00:17:52.071 --> 00:17:53.406
Thank you.

364
00:17:53.472 --> 00:17:55.741
I'm not standing here

365
00:17:56.309 --> 00:17:59.512
because I'm the best boxer in the room.

366
00:18:00.313 --> 00:18:02.782
I'm standing here
as a gym owner, a promoter,

367
00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:05.284
and the creator of this show.

368
00:18:05.351 --> 00:18:09.622
I prepared this stage in the hope of
reviving the spirit of boxing once again.

369
00:18:10.323 --> 00:18:13.726
Let the world see how exciting

370
00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:16.362
and thrilling boxing can be.

371
00:18:16.429 --> 00:18:17.563
That's all I ask.

372
00:18:18.364 --> 00:18:19.365
Are you all ready?

373
00:18:19.432 --> 00:18:21.767
- Yes!
- All right. Best of luck.

374
00:18:21.834 --> 00:18:25.504
It's incredible
what he is doing for boxing.

375
00:18:26.105 --> 00:18:28.975
I have mad respect for him.

376
00:18:29.742 --> 00:18:31.644
He's genuinely passionate about the sport.

377
00:18:31.711 --> 00:18:35.081
Everyone seemed to respect him
for his passion for boxing.

378
00:18:35.147 --> 00:18:39.352
The future of Korean boxing
rests on his shoulders.

379
00:18:39.418 --> 00:18:44.156
I would say Don Lee might love boxing
even more than I do.

380
00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:49.295
{\an8}When you see him in movies,
his punches are nearly flawless.

381
00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:55.901
He always incorporates boxing techniques
into his action sequences.

382
00:18:55.968 --> 00:18:59.338
It's clear that his understanding
of boxing runs deep.

383
00:18:59.405 --> 00:19:04.176
Thank goodness Don Lee didn't pursue
a professional career in boxing.

384
00:19:04.243 --> 00:19:07.013
If he had, we would've been rivals.

385
00:19:07.079 --> 00:19:10.549
I'm so grateful to him.
I'll be cheering for the show all the way.

386
00:19:10.616 --> 00:19:13.853
I have no doubt
it's going to be a huge success.

387
00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.956
[Lee] All right then, let's bring out

388
00:19:17.023 --> 00:19:19.158
the two hosts who'll be joining us

389
00:19:19.625 --> 00:19:21.627
on <i>I Am Boxer.</i>

390
00:19:22.762 --> 00:19:25.498
- [contestants exclaiming]
- Come on up.

391
00:19:29.201 --> 00:19:31.937
Hello, I'm Kim Jongkook,
one of the hosts of <i>I Am Boxer</i>.

392
00:19:32.004 --> 00:19:35.074
- Nice to meet you all.
- Oh, come on.

393
00:19:35.141 --> 00:19:38.010
Hello, I'm Dex,
the other host of <i>I Am Boxer</i>.

394
00:19:38.744 --> 00:19:40.146
Looking good!

395
00:19:40.212 --> 00:19:42.114
Looks like this show's gonna be a hit.

396
00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:43.482
The host lineup's amazing.

397
00:19:43.549 --> 00:19:48.621
<i>I Am Boxer</i> features a series of fights
that push every boxer to their limits.

398
00:19:49.088 --> 00:19:51.323
All contestants must fight for survival,

399
00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:54.160
regardless of weight class, age,

400
00:19:54.727 --> 00:19:56.295
or profession.

401
00:19:56.362 --> 00:19:59.999
Just a straight-up fight.
That's badass, just how it should be.

402
00:20:00.066 --> 00:20:02.001
It was thrilling.

403
00:20:02.068 --> 00:20:04.336
I could be up against
someone like Myung Hyunman

404
00:20:04.904 --> 00:20:06.872
or even Kim Donghoe.

405
00:20:06.939 --> 00:20:08.474
Well, I'm here.

406
00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:11.777
[in English]
There's no backing out now. Let's do it.

407
00:20:11.844 --> 00:20:15.981
[in Korean] Now, this is a big one.

408
00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:20.286
The winner of <i>I Am Boxer</i> will receive

409
00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:21.987
a champion belt...

410
00:20:27.493 --> 00:20:29.995
and a top-of-the-line flagship SUV.

411
00:20:30.062 --> 00:20:32.565
[contestants exclaiming]

412
00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:36.836
And finally,

413
00:20:36.902 --> 00:20:38.404
a grand prize of...

414
00:20:38.871 --> 00:20:40.172
[imitates drumroll]

415
00:20:40.239 --> 00:20:42.842
- A hundred million won?
- Two hundred million?

416
00:20:43.776 --> 00:20:45.344
...three hundred million won!

417
00:20:45.411 --> 00:20:47.279
...three hundred million won!

418
00:20:47.346 --> 00:20:49.648
- Three hundred million?
- [laughing]

419
00:20:49.715 --> 00:20:51.083
Yay!

420
00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:54.386
I literally gasped.
I was honestly shocked.

421
00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:57.256
There isn't
a single professional boxer in Korea

422
00:20:57.323 --> 00:21:00.092
who can make a living solely from boxing.

423
00:21:00.159 --> 00:21:04.630
Typically, pros make
about 100,000 won per round.

424
00:21:05.264 --> 00:21:06.265
Pretty low, huh?

425
00:21:06.332 --> 00:21:08.701
If I win this,
I could actually quit boxing.

426
00:21:08.768 --> 00:21:10.269
I could pay off my loans.

427
00:21:11.337 --> 00:21:14.874
I thought, "I really want to win.
I want to win and open my own gym."

428
00:21:15.441 --> 00:21:17.543
All right, everyone.

429
00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.880
It's time to reveal the first round.

430
00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:24.950
Round 1 of <i>I Am Boxer</i> is...

431
00:21:26.218 --> 00:21:27.953
the One-on-One Showdown.

432
00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.222
...the One-on-One Showdown.

433
00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:33.159
[contestants gasping, murmuring]

434
00:21:33.225 --> 00:21:35.161
Right from the start, huh?

435
00:21:38.364 --> 00:21:40.266
[Lee] The One-on-One Showdown

436
00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.335
will take place across nine rings.

437
00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:47.239
It is a head-to-head fight.

438
00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:50.910
Half of us will get cut, then.

439
00:21:52.278 --> 00:21:54.914
I thought,
"It's time to throw down for real."

440
00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:59.118
This is exactly what I wanted.
To fight to the end.

441
00:21:59.685 --> 00:22:01.020
It'll be a hell of a fight.

442
00:22:01.086 --> 00:22:03.088
My adrenaline was kicking in.

443
00:22:03.589 --> 00:22:08.561
The ring I'd like to choose is...
Ring No. 2. Ring No. 4. Ring No. 8.

444
00:22:08.627 --> 00:22:11.263
[Lee] Once the Master selects
one of the nine rings,

445
00:22:11.831 --> 00:22:14.533
- the fight begins immediately.
- [bell rings]

446
00:22:16.669 --> 00:22:18.838
The One-on-One showdown

447
00:22:18.904 --> 00:22:22.041
is a single match with no rounds.

448
00:22:23.909 --> 00:22:25.377
- That sounds tough.
- Yeah.

449
00:22:27.413 --> 00:22:28.647
[Lee] And the time limit is...

450
00:22:30.649 --> 00:22:33.419
- [contestant] Two minutes?
- [contestant] Three minutes?

451
00:22:34.887 --> 00:22:36.488
- [Lee] There isn't one.
- What?

452
00:22:36.555 --> 00:22:37.590
[Lee] There isn't one.

453
00:22:38.958 --> 00:22:41.227
- We just keep fighting then?
- Are they crazy?

454
00:22:41.293 --> 00:22:43.028
You're kidding, right?

455
00:22:43.095 --> 00:22:46.465
We'll need, like,
ten ambulances standing by for this.

456
00:22:46.532 --> 00:22:50.035
- No way. Is this for real?
- They want us to fight till we drop.

457
00:22:51.804 --> 00:22:53.372
So, it only ends when someone drops?

458
00:22:54.173 --> 00:22:55.641
No time limit?

459
00:22:56.108 --> 00:22:57.643
Honestly, that got me excited.

460
00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:00.880
Unlimited time? I love it.

461
00:23:00.946 --> 00:23:02.114
I absolutely love it.

462
00:23:03.315 --> 00:23:05.317
- [bell rings]
- [Lee] The fight continues...

463
00:23:06.619 --> 00:23:07.887
All right, let's stop here.

464
00:23:07.953 --> 00:23:10.489
[Lee] ...until the Master calls it.

465
00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:17.429
When the fight ends,
Master Don Lee will choose the winner.

466
00:23:17.496 --> 00:23:20.266
- So the Master's like a god?
- This is just like <i>Squid Game</i>.

467
00:23:21.367 --> 00:23:23.802
[Lee] The contestant not chosen
by the Master

468
00:23:24.603 --> 00:23:28.507
is immediately eliminated from <i>I Am Boxer.</i>

469
00:23:29.275 --> 00:23:30.609
That's harsh.

470
00:23:31.477 --> 00:23:32.645
That's just harsh.

471
00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:37.416
[Lee] Round 1 of <i>I Am Boxer</i>,

472
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.318
the One-on-One Showdown,

473
00:23:40.052 --> 00:23:41.553
starts now.

474
00:23:50.462 --> 00:23:52.164
We actually get to see this, huh?

475
00:23:52.231 --> 00:23:53.599
- I know.
- I know, right?

476
00:23:53.666 --> 00:23:55.167
- It's amazing.
- It's a festival.

477
00:23:55.234 --> 00:23:56.535
- Yeah, it really is.
- [laughing]

478
00:23:56.602 --> 00:23:59.238
- Boxing fans are gonna lose their minds.
- Definitely.

479
00:23:59.738 --> 00:24:02.608
[Lee] Before we begin
the One-on-One Showdown,

480
00:24:02.675 --> 00:24:05.911
please welcome the referees.

481
00:24:05.978 --> 00:24:08.847
[contestants exclaiming, applauding]

482
00:24:11.917 --> 00:24:13.953
[Dex] How cool.

483
00:24:14.019 --> 00:24:15.554
How many are there?

484
00:24:18.791 --> 00:24:21.493
I actually have a referee license myself.

485
00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.629
You have to box
for over 20 years to get one.

486
00:24:24.196 --> 00:24:27.599
- So referees can fight too?
- That's right. [laughing]

487
00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:30.903
Wow, that's what you took from that?

488
00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:32.771
No, I was just curious.

489
00:24:32.838 --> 00:24:35.774
[Lee] Round 1 of <i>I Am Boxer</i>,

490
00:24:35.841 --> 00:24:38.110
the One-on-One Showdown.

491
00:24:38.177 --> 00:24:40.679
Now, let's reveal the first matchup.

492
00:24:41.947 --> 00:24:43.716
I'm nervous.

493
00:24:43.782 --> 00:24:45.918
- [grunts]
- [contestants exclaiming, cheering]

494
00:24:45.985 --> 00:24:48.887
