- Did I hear a rope snap?

949
00:45:34.365 --> 00:45:35.566
That sounds heavy.

950
00:45:35.633 --> 00:45:36.767
I heard something break.

951
00:45:37.935 --> 00:45:39.370
His reach is insane.

952
00:45:40.404 --> 00:45:42.540
How do you close the distance? Oh, look.

953
00:45:48.946 --> 00:45:50.181
[contestant] Oh, that's a heavy shot.

954
00:45:51.249 --> 00:45:53.251
God, his punches are so heavy.

955
00:46:04.128 --> 00:46:05.296
Come on, you got this!

956
00:46:06.063 --> 00:46:07.164
[contestant 2] He's good.

957
00:46:07.231 --> 00:46:08.266
Julien's good.

958
00:46:10.034 --> 00:46:11.335
[contestant 3] Oh, he's going in.

959
00:46:13.704 --> 00:46:14.972
- [referee] Stop!
- Oh, goodness.

960
00:46:15.039 --> 00:46:17.575
{\an8}- Damn.
- [contestant 4] That's got to hurt bad.

961
00:46:17.642 --> 00:46:19.110
Three...

962
00:46:19.176 --> 00:46:22.213
[Hyunmin] When I took that heavy punch
in the face,

963
00:46:22.280 --> 00:46:23.314
I was completely dazed.

964
00:46:23.381 --> 00:46:26.951
I've never been hit that hard in my life.

965
00:46:27.485 --> 00:46:29.920
I thought I was getting smashed
with a baseball bat.

966
00:46:29.987 --> 00:46:31.055
Seriously.

967
00:46:31.122 --> 00:46:32.857
You put your guard up, right?

968
00:46:32.923 --> 00:46:35.092
But when you realize
how powerful the punches are,

969
00:46:35.159 --> 00:46:36.861
- you stop attacking.
- [Dex] Ah...

970
00:46:36.927 --> 00:46:38.729
- You just keep your guard up.
- You freeze.

971
00:46:38.796 --> 00:46:39.864
Yeah, you can't help it.

972
00:46:39.930 --> 00:46:41.432
[contestant] Man, that looks brutal.

973
00:46:41.499 --> 00:46:42.967
[contestant 2] He's living up
to his reputation.

974
00:46:43.601 --> 00:46:44.969
Step forward. Can you continue?

975
00:46:45.036 --> 00:46:46.103
- Yes.
- Okay.

976
00:46:46.170 --> 00:46:47.471
[contestant] Yes, push through.

977
00:46:47.538 --> 00:46:49.006
Just land one shot. Just one.

978
00:46:49.073 --> 00:46:50.741
Fighting till the end is what matters.

979
00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:52.576
[contestant 2] Press in
and land one clean hit.

980
00:46:52.643 --> 00:46:54.979
- [contestant 3] He's got to go in! Go in!
- [contestant 4] Go!

981
00:46:55.046 --> 00:46:56.047
Shoot, too short.

982
00:46:56.113 --> 00:46:57.381
[contestant 5] Man, that reach!

983
00:46:58.115 --> 00:46:59.317
It's his physique.

984
00:47:01.485 --> 00:47:02.520
[referee] Break!

985
00:47:06.023 --> 00:47:07.625
- Come on, you got this.
- [Lee] Come on.

986
00:47:08.426 --> 00:47:10.127
[contestant] Come on, let's go!

987
00:47:12.330 --> 00:47:13.331
Break!

988
00:47:16.801 --> 00:47:18.569
- [bell dings]
- Stop!

989
00:47:18.636 --> 00:47:20.504
[announcer] <i>The fight is over.</i>

990
00:47:20.571 --> 00:47:22.540
[contestant] So this is what Julien Kang
is made of.

991
00:47:22.606 --> 00:47:23.607
He's strong.

992
00:47:24.108 --> 00:47:26.344
You can really feel the weight
behind his punches.

993
00:47:26.410 --> 00:47:29.980
For the first time in the ring,
I actually heard something tear.

994
00:47:30.047 --> 00:47:31.515
Sounded like the ring collapsing.

995
00:47:32.817 --> 00:47:34.151
[metal clangs]

996
00:47:35.152 --> 00:47:36.854
- [contestant] Oh, my goodness.
- Break!

997
00:47:36.921 --> 00:47:41.192
I think "intimidating" is the best word
to describe this match.

998
00:47:41.258 --> 00:47:42.993
It really was intimidating.

999
00:47:43.928 --> 00:47:46.130
Julien is definitely a tough one to beat.

1000
00:47:46.897 --> 00:47:47.965
[contestants applauding]

1001
00:47:48.032 --> 00:47:51.535
{\an8}RED CORNER JULIEN KANG SURVIVES

1002
00:47:51.602 --> 00:47:52.803
[contestant] He really is a top fighter.

1003
00:47:52.870 --> 00:47:54.338
He proved himself.

1004
00:47:55.239 --> 00:47:56.640
He's just as good as they say.

1005
00:47:56.707 --> 00:47:58.909
[contestant 2] Man,
these matchups are fire.

1006
00:47:59.410 --> 00:48:01.712
But the more I watch and see the winners,

1007
00:48:01.779 --> 00:48:03.781
the more I start to freak out. [chuckles]

1008
00:48:04.281 --> 00:48:08.319
Feels like we're left
with the real heavy-hitters now.

1009
00:48:08.386 --> 00:48:10.688
What's left are wars to be fought.

1010
00:48:11.522 --> 00:48:12.757
They're all outstanding.

1011
00:48:13.758 --> 00:48:15.326
[Jongkook] Oh, are we gonna go there?

1012
00:48:18.329 --> 00:48:19.497
My next pick is...

1013
00:48:19.563 --> 00:48:21.866
[contestant] Oh, I'm nervous.
This is nerve-racking!

1014
00:48:23.701 --> 00:48:25.035
Oh, man...

1015
00:48:26.504 --> 00:48:29.173
[producer] Do you have a top contender
in mind?

1016
00:48:29.240 --> 00:48:30.241
Kim Donghoe.

1017
00:48:30.307 --> 00:48:33.077
He's hit the peak as an amateur boxer.

1018
00:48:33.144 --> 00:48:34.345
Probably the best in Korea.

1019
00:48:34.412 --> 00:48:35.913
He's definitely a top contender.

1020
00:48:35.980 --> 00:48:37.782
- Donghoe.
- [producer chuckles]

1021
00:48:40.284 --> 00:48:43.220
I swear, I'm only good at boxing.

1022
00:48:43.921 --> 00:48:47.391
[contestant] He's going for his 14th win
at the National Sports Festival.

1023
00:48:48.692 --> 00:48:52.930
Whether I'm up against a friend
or a junior, I fight to win.

1024
00:48:53.597 --> 00:48:56.233
[Dawoon] This is my first time seeing
Kim Donghoe fight.

1025
00:48:56.300 --> 00:48:59.336
I've heard his name a thousand times.

1026
00:48:59.403 --> 00:49:01.972
People call him
"Son Goku from Dragon Ball".

1027
00:49:02.039 --> 00:49:03.707
- Is that so?
- Among the amateur boxers.

1028
00:49:03.774 --> 00:49:06.444
[announcer] <i>The 14-time consecutive
champion of the National Sports Festival,</i>

1029
00:49:06.510 --> 00:49:08.412
<i>representing Boryeong City Hall,
Kim Donghoe!</i>

1030
00:49:09.947 --> 00:49:11.916
[Sangsoo] I mean, seriously...

1031
00:49:11.982 --> 00:49:13.517
I couldn't help but laugh.

1032
00:49:14.051 --> 00:49:16.487
I mean, come on...

1033
00:49:16.554 --> 00:49:19.690
You matched me up with the final boss.

1034
00:49:19.757 --> 00:49:21.025
It's just cruel.

1035
00:49:21.559 --> 00:49:24.728
But still, I am an MMA fighter.

1036
00:49:24.795 --> 00:49:28.032
I wanted to face him properly once.
For pride's sake, you know?

1037
00:49:28.098 --> 00:49:30.801
[announcer] <i>From the blue corner,
the former World Sambo Champion,</i>

1038
00:49:30.868 --> 00:49:33.904
- <i>King of Endurance, Lee Sangsoo!</i>
- [contestant] King of Endurance.

1039
00:49:33.971 --> 00:49:35.206
FORMER WORLD SAMBO CHAMPION

1040
00:49:35.272 --> 00:49:37.107
Is he someone famous too?

1041
00:49:37.174 --> 00:49:38.242
Sangsoo?

1042
00:49:38.309 --> 00:49:41.345
- He's a veteran in combat sports.
- Really?

1043
00:49:41.412 --> 00:49:43.080
He started with judo, then sambo,

1044
00:49:43.147 --> 00:49:44.515
then MMA.

1045
00:49:44.582 --> 00:49:46.617
I participated in
the "World Sambo Championship"

1046
00:49:47.184 --> 00:49:49.186
{\an8}and won it three years in a row.

1047
00:49:49.253 --> 00:49:52.456
{\an8}I came here to prove I've still got it.

1048
00:49:52.523 --> 00:49:55.459
- Sangsoo is known as King of Endurance.
- That's right.

1049
00:49:55.526 --> 00:49:58.629
I should know.
I've tested his tolerance myself.

1050
00:49:59.263 --> 00:50:01.098
{\an8}KIM JONGKOOK

1051
00:50:02.199 --> 00:50:03.200
{\an8}MYUNG HYUNMAN

1052
00:50:03.267 --> 00:50:04.535
{\an8}JAY PARK, JULIEN KANG

1053
00:50:04.602 --> 00:50:06.303
{\an8}ALEX PEREIRA

1054
00:50:07.271 --> 00:50:08.405
Wow, that's rough!

1055
00:50:09.139 --> 00:50:11.542
[Sangsoo] My abs can withstand anything.

1056
00:50:11.609 --> 00:50:13.210
Go ahead, take your shot.

1057
00:50:15.012 --> 00:50:16.080
{\an8}[Jongkook] Offense versus defense.

1058
00:50:16.146 --> 00:50:18.215
{\an8}[Lee] A matchup
between the living legends.

1059
00:50:18.282 --> 00:50:22.720
People would want to see
if he can still hold up in the ring.

1060
00:50:22.786 --> 00:50:23.787
Right.

1061
00:50:23.854 --> 00:50:26.156
- Against one of the best boxers too.
- Exactly.

1062
00:50:26.223 --> 00:50:28.259
[Donghoe] I bet
every fighter here knows me.

1063
00:50:28.325 --> 00:50:30.327
I've got to live up to their expectations.

1064
00:50:30.928 --> 00:50:34.365
I know he can take hits,
so how do I crack him?

1065
00:50:35.432 --> 00:50:38.702
[Sangsoo] Korean boxing isn't yet
on the same level as the global scene.

1066
00:50:38.769 --> 00:50:42.706
I'll show you what world-class looks like.

1067
00:50:42.773 --> 00:50:43.807
Ring No. 5.

1068
00:50:45.576 --> 00:50:47.177
- Box.
- [bell dings]

1069
00:50:47.244 --> 00:50:49.446
[contestants] Let's go! Go, go!

1070
00:50:50.614 --> 00:50:52.883
[contestants] Let's go! Go, go!

1071
00:51:00.357 --> 00:51:01.358
Damn, he's fast.

1072
00:51:06.864 --> 00:51:07.998
[contestants gasping]

1073
00:51:12.603 --> 00:51:14.538
Wow, great rhythm and timing.

1074
00:51:16.540 --> 00:51:19.043
Okay!

1075
00:51:19.843 --> 00:51:22.046
- His punches land so smoothly.
- Yes, they're heavy.

1076
00:51:22.112 --> 00:51:23.380
[contestant] That's beautiful.

1077
00:51:25.482 --> 00:51:27.351
[contestant 2] Go in.
You have to go for it.

1078
00:51:31.255 --> 00:51:32.256
- Whoa.
- Nice!

1079
00:51:38.095 --> 00:51:39.096
Nice.

1080
00:51:39.163 --> 00:51:40.931
Wow, Sangsoo's doing well.

1081
00:51:40.998 --> 00:51:42.032
- Not bad at all.
- Yeah.

1082
00:51:46.136 --> 00:51:47.371
[Lee] He's leaving his body open.

1083
00:51:47.438 --> 00:51:48.639
Whoa, he's...

1084
00:51:52.076 --> 00:51:53.677
[contestant] Because body shots
don't affect him.

1085
00:51:54.345 --> 00:51:57.281
[Donghoe] I've always been confident
in my punches, so I went for his body,

1086
00:51:57.848 --> 00:51:59.483
but he didn't even flinch.

1087
00:52:00.317 --> 00:52:02.519
[Lee] He's taking those body shots
like it's nothing.

1088
00:52:02.586 --> 00:52:04.722
- He should stop going for the body.
- [chuckles]

1089
00:52:04.788 --> 00:52:05.923
It's a waste of energy.

1090
00:52:08.926 --> 00:52:10.928
[contestants exclaiming]

1091
00:52:10.995 --> 00:52:13.497
[Kim Donghoe]
I realized body shots wouldn't work,

1092
00:52:13.564 --> 00:52:16.967
so I switched it up
and went for the head instead.

1093
00:52:25.209 --> 00:52:26.543
[contestant] Oh, boy.

1094
00:52:26.610 --> 00:52:27.678
That's good.

1095
00:52:29.747 --> 00:52:31.882
How does he move like that?

1096
00:52:32.950 --> 00:52:34.084
Let's go, Lee Sangsoo!

1097
00:52:34.151 --> 00:52:35.552
- You got this!
- You got this!

1098
00:52:36.787 --> 00:52:38.789
He's not missing a single punch.

1099
00:52:38.856 --> 00:52:40.658
[contestant] Damn, he's good.

1100
00:52:46.463 --> 00:52:48.332
There it is. His signature move.

1101
00:52:49.066 --> 00:52:50.567
[contestants exclaiming]

1102
00:52:50.634 --> 00:52:52.436
He keeps firing from every stance.

1103
00:52:52.503 --> 00:52:54.905
He's super skillful.

1104
00:53:02.546 --> 00:53:03.580
Stop!

1105
00:53:03.647 --> 00:53:05.549
- [announcer] <i>The fight is over.</i>
- [contestants exclaiming]

1106
00:53:05.616 --> 00:53:07.184
That's pure art.

1107
00:53:07.951 --> 00:53:10.254
He makes it look so effortless.

1108
00:53:10.320 --> 00:53:12.690
We were supposed to be talking,

1109
00:53:12.756 --> 00:53:14.324
but my jaw just dropped.

1110
00:53:14.391 --> 00:53:16.226
I just sat there speechless.

1111
00:53:16.293 --> 00:53:18.862
- He wouldn't go for my body.
- [judges laughing]

1112
00:53:19.463 --> 00:53:20.998
[Sangsoo] He faked it,

1113
00:53:21.065 --> 00:53:22.332
then went straight for my face.

1114
00:53:22.833 --> 00:53:24.201
He was amazing.

1115
00:53:24.268 --> 00:53:26.103
I did throw a few body shots.

1116
00:53:26.170 --> 00:53:28.472
Most people flinch, but not him.

1117
00:53:28.539 --> 00:53:30.708
He kept coming like it was nothing,
so I was shocked.

1118
00:53:30.774 --> 00:53:32.409
Nothing gets through Sangsoo's body.

1119
00:53:32.476 --> 00:53:33.877
[laughing]

1120
00:53:33.944 --> 00:53:35.779
He's a legend for a reason, though.

1121
00:53:35.846 --> 00:53:38.315
His punches look light,
but they're insanely powerful.

1122
00:53:38.382 --> 00:53:39.983
[contestant] Oh, really?

1123
00:53:40.050 --> 00:53:42.352
They did look light.
I guess they're heavy.

1124
00:53:42.419 --> 00:53:45.456
He puts even more weight
behind his punches by relaxing his body.

1125
00:53:45.522 --> 00:53:49.259
All right, so the survivor of this match
is Kim Donghoe from the red corner.

1126
00:53:49.326 --> 00:53:51.762
[contestants exclaiming, applauding]

1127
00:53:55.833 --> 00:53:57.034
The Boxing Ghost.

1128
00:53:59.036 --> 00:54:00.037
[Lee] And finally...

1129
00:54:01.338 --> 00:54:02.873
Okay, here we go.

1130
00:54:02.940 --> 00:54:04.341
It's time.

1131
00:54:04.408 --> 00:54:05.776
The main event of the day.

1132
00:54:06.410 --> 00:54:07.845
This one's going to be intense.

1133
00:54:08.412 --> 00:54:10.481
You're telling me these fighters are here?

1134
00:54:10.547 --> 00:54:12.015
They are top-tier fighters.

1135
00:54:12.616 --> 00:54:13.751
[contestant] The current champion.

1136
00:54:13.817 --> 00:54:16.120
- He's the East Asia champion, right?
- Yeah.

1137
00:54:16.186 --> 00:54:17.688
The former versus the current.

1138
00:54:17.755 --> 00:54:19.289
This feels like the finals already.

1139
00:54:19.356 --> 00:54:21.291
- This one's got to be the most fun.
- Definitely.

1140
00:54:22.493 --> 00:54:24.294
I'll choose Ring No. 6.

1141
00:54:24.361 --> 00:54:26.096
- The legends.
- This is gonna be fun.

1142
00:54:26.163 --> 00:54:27.898
This could be a historic match.

1143
00:54:27.965 --> 00:54:30.134
[announcer] <i>From the blue corner,
Korea's reigning featherweight</i>

1144
00:54:30.200 --> 00:54:33.403
<i>and East Asia lightweight champion,
Kim Taesun.</i>

1145
00:54:33.470 --> 00:54:34.571
[contestants exclaiming]

1146
00:54:34.638 --> 00:54:36.540
He's a rising star.

1147
00:54:36.607 --> 00:54:38.408
His stamina is insane, and he's fierce.

1148
00:54:38.475 --> 00:54:40.577
He just keeps pressing hard.

1149
00:54:40.644 --> 00:54:43.113
[announcer] <i>From the red corner,
former national team member</i>

1150
00:54:43.180 --> 00:54:46.383
<i>and East Asia
super lightweight champion, Kim Minuk.</i>

1151
00:54:46.450 --> 00:54:48.452
- [contestant] It's Snyper!
- [contestants exclaiming]

1152
00:54:49.419 --> 00:54:52.923
Honestly, Kim Minuk was
one of my all-time favorites.

1153
00:54:52.990 --> 00:54:53.991
Snyper, huh?

1154
00:54:54.057 --> 00:54:57.194
I don't follow boxing closely,
but I know who Kim Minuk is.

1155
00:54:57.261 --> 00:54:58.962
You could say he's a star boxer.

1156
00:54:59.029 --> 00:55:00.898
Who will win, the old or the new champion?

1157
00:55:03.500 --> 00:55:07.070
I'm the current WBA Asia East champion
and the Korean super featherweight champ,

1158
00:55:07.137 --> 00:55:09.907
defending my title for the fourth time.

1159
00:55:09.973 --> 00:55:11.508
Go in, go in!

1160
00:55:12.276 --> 00:55:14.211
[commentator 1] Okay!
This is a battle of pride!

1161
00:55:14.711 --> 00:55:17.915
- [commentator 2] Oh, he stopped the match!
- The referee put a stop to it!

1162
00:55:17.981 --> 00:55:19.883
[Taesun] My record so far is 13 wins,

1163
00:55:19.950 --> 00:55:23.821
9 by KO, 3 losses,
and 2 draws in 18 fights.

1164
00:55:23.887 --> 00:55:27.858
I'm a former national team player
and a previous East Asian champion.

1165
00:55:27.925 --> 00:55:29.827
[commentator 1] He's got him in a bind!

1166
00:55:29.893 --> 00:55:31.595
- He is down!
- [commentator 2] Congratulations!

1167
00:55:31.662 --> 00:55:33.831
That was Kim Minuk
of the Republic of Korea!

1168
00:55:33.897 --> 00:55:36.033
And he is now
the super featherweight champion!

1169
00:55:36.867 --> 00:55:40.604
[Minuk] My record is 16 wins,
12 by KO, and 1 loss.

1170
00:55:41.672 --> 00:55:44.374
I got the nickname "Snyper"

1171
00:55:44.441 --> 00:55:46.777
because I score knockouts
with straight punches.

1172
00:55:46.844 --> 00:55:50.113
That's why people started calling me that.

1173
00:55:50.180 --> 00:55:52.049
I'll show you
how I made a name for myself.

1174
00:55:52.115 --> 00:55:54.718
Come on then, bring it on.
I'll finish you off, sir.

1175
00:55:55.118 --> 00:55:58.121
{\an8}KIM MINUK VERSUS KIM TAESUN

1176
00:55:58.755 --> 00:55:59.923
This is going to be good.

1177
00:55:59.990 --> 00:56:02.226
I'm going to get a closer look.

1178
00:56:02.292 --> 00:56:03.560
You don't see this every day.

1179
00:56:05.696 --> 00:56:06.697
[chuckles]

1180
00:56:08.799 --> 00:56:11.768
- There's an age gap, so who knows?
- Right.

1181
00:56:11.835 --> 00:56:13.871
Kim Minuk has his moves,
so you never know.

1182
00:56:13.937 --> 00:56:15.572
One of them is gonna take a serious hit.

1183
00:56:15.639 --> 00:56:18.075
I feel like Taesun might take a hit.

1184
00:56:19.009 --> 00:56:20.677
I don't know. We'll have to see.

1185
00:56:20.744 --> 00:56:22.579
[contestant sighs] This is intense.

1186
00:56:23.947 --> 00:56:25.015
[sighs]

1187
00:56:26.717 --> 00:56:28.518
All right, Ring No. 6.

1188
00:56:29.086 --> 00:56:30.220
Why am I feeling nervous?

1189
00:56:31.755 --> 00:56:32.823
[Minuk clears throat]

1190
00:56:35.425 --> 00:56:36.593
- Box.
- [bell rings]

1191
00:56:36.660 --> 00:56:39.229
- [contestant 1] Let's go!
- [contestant 2] You got this!

1192
00:56:49.106 --> 00:56:50.374
Even the air feels heavier.

1193
00:56:53.043 --> 00:56:54.811
[contestants exclaiming]

1194
00:56:57.814 --> 00:56:59.082
It's fine. He rolled with it.

1195
00:57:02.786 --> 00:57:05.689
- [grunting]
- His defense is solid.

1196
00:57:05.756 --> 00:57:07.457
He's not missing anything.

1197
00:57:08.125 --> 00:57:10.160
- Watch out for body shots.
- [contestants exclaim]

1198
00:57:10.227 --> 00:57:11.962
- Watch out for body shots.
- [contestants exclaim]

1199
00:57:12.029 --> 00:57:14.064
- That was a clean hit.
- That's Snyper for you.

1200
00:57:15.365 --> 00:57:16.600
He's totally composed.

1201
00:57:17.367 --> 00:57:18.769
He's like, "Come at me."

1202
00:57:18.835 --> 00:57:20.270
[contestants exclaiming]

1203
00:57:22.706 --> 00:57:24.207
He's making it fun.

1204
00:57:24.274 --> 00:57:25.342
[contestant laughs]

1205
00:57:30.047 --> 00:57:31.214
Man, that's a good punch.

1206
00:57:32.816 --> 00:57:33.884
That's insane.

1207
00:57:33.951 --> 00:57:35.485
He's still got it.

1208
00:57:35.552 --> 00:57:37.354
- Those punches sound like gunshots.
- Yeah.

1209
00:57:37.421 --> 00:57:39.823
I think Minuk's punches are more powerful.

1210
00:57:46.430 --> 00:57:47.898
- He just plants it in.
- He's fast.

1211
00:57:47.965 --> 00:57:50.267
Man, Kim Taesun's good.

1212
00:57:50.767 --> 00:57:53.570
I took a hit to the body. It hurt.

1213
00:57:54.137 --> 00:57:56.206
I let my guard down
for a split second and got hit

1214
00:57:56.273 --> 00:57:58.976
just as I was inhaling.

1215
00:58:01.578 --> 00:58:02.679
[grunting]

1216
00:58:05.515 --> 00:58:06.917
