01:08:35.445 --> 01:08:37.246
- To your corners.
- [announcer] <i>The fight is over.</i>

1462
01:08:37.313 --> 01:08:38.615
He's got great body shots.

1463
01:08:39.015 --> 01:08:41.484
He's got the reach to hit from a distance.

1464
01:08:41.551 --> 01:08:42.552
He's so cool.

1465
01:08:45.188 --> 01:08:49.292
I think these two just gave us
the most explosive match yet.

1466
01:08:49.359 --> 01:08:50.760
Yeah, as expected.

1467
01:08:50.827 --> 01:08:52.261
[Seongjun] I got pounded good.

1468
01:08:52.328 --> 01:08:55.632
Made me wonder if this was the difference
between boxing and MMA.

1469
01:08:57.467 --> 01:08:59.936
The survivor of this match is...

1470
01:09:00.503 --> 01:09:02.739
Kuk Seungjun from the red corner.

1471
01:09:04.374 --> 01:09:05.508
Congratulations.

1472
01:09:08.344 --> 01:09:12.081
[Seongjun] I thought he was just an actor
who boxed for fun.

1473
01:09:12.649 --> 01:09:14.317
But turns out he's the real deal.

1474
01:09:14.384 --> 01:09:15.518
I got pummeled out there.

1475
01:09:20.857 --> 01:09:23.793
[Lee] The ring I'm choosing next is...

1476
01:09:24.360 --> 01:09:25.962
[contestant 1] Yoon Hyeongbin, perhaps?

1477
01:09:26.696 --> 01:09:28.264
[contestant 2] Come on, Ring No. 6.

1478
01:09:28.331 --> 01:09:31.968
Comedian-turned-MMA-fighter Yoon Hyeongbin

1479
01:09:32.935 --> 01:09:36.673
and rising pro boxer Kim Jaewon.

1480
01:09:36.739 --> 01:09:39.075
Let's watch their match next.

1481
01:09:39.142 --> 01:09:40.677
{\an8}YOON HYEONGBIN VERSUS KIM JAEWON

1482
01:09:40.743 --> 01:09:41.778
{\an8}This is gonna be fun.

1483
01:09:42.245 --> 01:09:44.080
- Hyeongbin's amazing.
- Awesome.

1484
01:09:44.647 --> 01:09:47.083
Let's do this!

1485
01:09:47.150 --> 01:09:48.785
[cheering]

1486
01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:49.852
Go, man!

1487
01:09:51.220 --> 01:09:53.189
Officially speaking,

1488
01:09:53.256 --> 01:09:56.292
I've got a 100% win rate
and a 100% KO rate.

1489
01:09:56.359 --> 01:09:58.728
I'm the real <i>One-Punch Man</i>.

1490
01:09:58.795 --> 01:10:00.463
Brush my fist and you hit the deck.

1491
01:10:01.698 --> 01:10:04.467
I always win with my punches.

1492
01:10:04.534 --> 01:10:07.503
As a fighter, I believe I can beat anyone.

1493
01:10:07.570 --> 01:10:08.738
I'm confident.

1494
01:10:10.440 --> 01:10:11.774
[Jaewon] My punch hits different.

1495
01:10:11.841 --> 01:10:13.843
No one else can compare.

1496
01:10:15.445 --> 01:10:17.513
I've got one-hit power.

1497
01:10:17.580 --> 01:10:20.349
My fists may be smaller,
but I can take someone out in one shot.

1498
01:10:20.817 --> 01:10:22.385
He's quite strong, actually.

1499
01:10:22.852 --> 01:10:24.420
It's a one-punch kind of match, huh?

1500
01:10:24.487 --> 01:10:25.488
You're right.

1501
01:10:26.022 --> 01:10:27.223
[Lee] Ring No. 2.

1502
01:10:28.591 --> 01:10:29.859
Box.

1503
01:10:29.926 --> 01:10:30.927
Box.

1504
01:10:30.993 --> 01:10:31.994
[bell rings]

1505
01:10:32.061 --> 01:10:33.229
- Yeah!
- Box!

1506
01:10:33.730 --> 01:10:35.498
They're going at it right away.

1507
01:10:42.505 --> 01:10:43.506
Break!

1508
01:10:43.573 --> 01:10:44.640
He's clinching.

1509
01:10:45.541 --> 01:10:46.542
Box!

1510
01:10:48.244 --> 01:10:50.046
That looks like holding and hitting.

1511
01:10:50.513 --> 01:10:52.849
- The clinch?
- That's a dirty boxing move.

1512
01:10:55.184 --> 01:10:56.753
Holding and hitting.

1513
01:10:57.220 --> 01:10:59.021
It's giving MMA vibes.

1514
01:10:59.088 --> 01:11:01.257
Fighting like that
will tire out your opponent fast.

1515
01:11:01.824 --> 01:11:04.527
[Hyeongbin]
That was just a part of the plan.

1516
01:11:04.594 --> 01:11:06.395
Start from mid-range,

1517
01:11:06.462 --> 01:11:07.830
go straight into a clinch,

1518
01:11:07.897 --> 01:11:09.532
wear him down, then break away.

1519
01:11:10.366 --> 01:11:11.868
Clinches really wear you out.

1520
01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:13.069
- They do.
- Yes.

1521
01:11:13.936 --> 01:11:15.304
He isn't giving him an opening.

1522
01:11:17.140 --> 01:11:20.409
[Jaewon] I wanted to keep my distance
and control the exchanges,

1523
01:11:20.476 --> 01:11:23.446
but he kept clinching and hammering me.

1524
01:11:23.513 --> 01:11:25.815
It felt like I couldn't show my skills.

1525
01:11:25.882 --> 01:11:26.883
Break.

1526
01:11:27.350 --> 01:11:28.551
He needs to move first.

1527
01:11:31.320 --> 01:11:32.355
[contestants exclaim]

1528
01:11:33.189 --> 01:11:34.857
Whoa, he's as strong as expected.

1529
01:11:34.924 --> 01:11:36.492
Dang, his punches.

1530
01:11:36.559 --> 01:11:38.227
He's going for it.

1531
01:11:38.795 --> 01:11:39.796
He took a hit.

1532
01:11:40.997 --> 01:11:43.399
Whoa, his power's no joke.

1533
01:11:47.336 --> 01:11:48.538
Keep going!

1534
01:11:52.575 --> 01:11:54.076
[contestants exclaim]

1535
01:11:54.143 --> 01:11:55.344
He keeps grabbing him.

1536
01:11:57.346 --> 01:11:58.714
Hyeongbin, let's go!

1537
01:11:58.781 --> 01:11:59.949
- Come on!
- That body shot!

1538
01:12:00.416 --> 01:12:02.552
That one landed.

1539
01:12:06.789 --> 01:12:09.225
Looks like Hyeongbin is getting tired.

1540
01:12:11.494 --> 01:12:12.995
[bell rings]

1541
01:12:13.062 --> 01:12:14.063
Stop!

1542
01:12:14.130 --> 01:12:15.431
[contestants applauding]

1543
01:12:15.498 --> 01:12:16.999
Who do you think will win?

1544
01:12:17.066 --> 01:12:18.935
[Lee sighs]

1545
01:12:19.402 --> 01:12:20.970
Who's he going to pick?

1546
01:12:21.771 --> 01:12:24.473
His clinch was solid, though.

1547
01:12:25.141 --> 01:12:28.077
It definitely threw the other off a bit.

1548
01:12:28.144 --> 01:12:30.346
How was the match, Jaewon?

1549
01:12:30.413 --> 01:12:33.349
Honestly, I could've done more.

1550
01:12:33.416 --> 01:12:35.518
- [chuckling]
- I really think I could've won.

1551
01:12:35.585 --> 01:12:38.154
I just got caught up in too many clinches.
I could've won.

1552
01:12:38.221 --> 01:12:40.156
- [laughing]
- That's honest of him.

1553
01:12:41.257 --> 01:12:44.360
I think clinching is
a skill in its own right.

1554
01:12:44.427 --> 01:12:46.495
- Yes, you're right.
- Right, right.

1555
01:12:47.530 --> 01:12:49.332
[Lee] The winner of this match is...

1556
01:12:55.738 --> 01:12:57.473
{\an8}Kim Jaewon from the blue corner.

1557
01:12:58.574 --> 01:12:59.609
{\an8}Thank you, sir!

1558
01:13:00.810 --> 01:13:02.645
- [Lee] Congratulations.
- Thank you!

1559
01:13:03.045 --> 01:13:04.580
- Congratulations.
- [Jaewon] Thank you!

1560
01:13:05.047 --> 01:13:07.383
Thank you. Great game.

1561
01:13:07.450 --> 01:13:10.119
- Great work.
- Well done.

1562
01:13:11.554 --> 01:13:14.323
[Lee] Now, let's move on to the two men
with incredible builds.

1563
01:13:14.924 --> 01:13:16.158
{\an8}Ring No. 3.

1564
01:13:16.225 --> 01:13:17.426
{\an8}[contestant] We've got bodybuilders.

1565
01:13:17.894 --> 01:13:19.228
It's like a bodybuilding contest.

1566
01:13:19.295 --> 01:13:21.864
What are they? Sports models?

1567
01:13:21.931 --> 01:13:23.099
Wow, amazing.

1568
01:13:23.165 --> 01:13:24.867
Which coconut shoulders will win?

1569
01:13:24.934 --> 01:13:26.869
- Box.
- Box!

1570
01:13:28.371 --> 01:13:30.273
[contestants clamoring]

1571
01:13:31.207 --> 01:13:33.409
- [exclaims]
- Whoa, they're good.

1572
01:13:33.476 --> 01:13:35.878
He's taking multiple uppercuts!

1573
01:13:35.945 --> 01:13:37.313
Are those abs made of iron?

1574
01:13:37.380 --> 01:13:38.547
He's done.

1575
01:13:38.614 --> 01:13:40.249
Park Youngho is really feisty.

1576
01:13:40.316 --> 01:13:42.418
{\an8}[Lee]
Park Youngho from the red corner wins.

1577
01:13:42.885 --> 01:13:44.487
Let's move on to Ring No. 7.

1578
01:13:45.588 --> 01:13:46.589
[contestant exclaims]

1579
01:13:46.656 --> 01:13:48.824
{\an8}O3OHN VERSUS KIM JONGOH

1580
01:13:48.891 --> 01:13:50.226
He looks like Jung Haein.

1581
01:13:51.027 --> 01:13:52.461
- He's good-looking.
- That's cute.

1582
01:13:53.229 --> 01:13:54.430
O3ohn!

1583
01:13:55.298 --> 01:13:56.799
Ah, a fellow singer.

1584
01:13:56.866 --> 01:13:58.034
[laughs]

1585
01:13:58.100 --> 01:14:00.569
I'll prove why I deserve to be here.

1586
01:14:00.636 --> 01:14:03.472
I'll show you my passion
and drive for boxing.

1587
01:14:03.539 --> 01:14:04.807
[bell rings]

1588
01:14:05.508 --> 01:14:06.642
Oh, he's strong.

1589
01:14:07.777 --> 01:14:11.781
That hairstyle and his moves
scream boxer from the '70s!

1590
01:14:15.885 --> 01:14:17.353
Wait, he's good.

1591
01:14:18.154 --> 01:14:19.455
Why is he good?

1592
01:14:22.892 --> 01:14:27.496
{\an8}[Lee] The winner of this match is
O3ohn from the red corner.

1593
01:14:28.898 --> 01:14:31.400
{\an8}Ring No. 6.
We have Kwon Asol and Hong Junyoung.

1594
01:14:31.467 --> 01:14:32.735
{\an8}KWON ASOL VERSUS HONG JUNYOUNG

1595
01:14:32.802 --> 01:14:34.236
This is a big match.

1596
01:14:36.038 --> 01:14:37.039
[contestants exclaiming]

1597
01:14:37.106 --> 01:14:38.140
Nice cross.

1598
01:14:39.408 --> 01:14:40.743
Nice!

1599
01:14:43.946 --> 01:14:46.482
- Hong Junyoung's got great footwork.
- [exclaiming]

1600
01:14:46.549 --> 01:14:48.384
He's also throwing a lot of punches.

1601
01:14:48.451 --> 01:14:50.386
Kwon Asol's going to tire out soon.

1602
01:14:54.523 --> 01:14:58.060
{\an8}[Lee]
The winner of this match is Hong Junyoung.

1603
01:14:59.762 --> 01:15:02.098
All right, folks.

1604
01:15:02.164 --> 01:15:05.334
Next up is the showdown
between Korea's two strongest.

1605
01:15:05.401 --> 01:15:06.435
{\an8}[contestants clamoring]

1606
01:15:06.502 --> 01:15:08.537
{\an8}MYUNG HYUNMAN VERSUS JUNG DAWOON

1607
01:15:08.604 --> 01:15:10.473
{\an8}- No way.
- This is insane!

1608
01:15:11.207 --> 01:15:13.876
- [exclaims]
- That's a scary sight.

1609
01:15:13.943 --> 01:15:14.944
Here we go.

1610
01:15:15.945 --> 01:15:17.146
Better watch this up close.

1611
01:15:18.647 --> 01:15:20.483
Let's watch from up here.

1612
01:15:20.549 --> 01:15:21.951
We can't miss this.

1613
01:15:22.018 --> 01:15:23.686
It's the main event!

1614
01:15:24.420 --> 01:15:26.355
Wow, this is incredible.

1615
01:15:27.356 --> 01:15:28.824
You can't see this anywhere else.

1616
01:15:29.291 --> 01:15:31.560
[Lee] Asia's top kickboxer...

1617
01:15:33.496 --> 01:15:35.831
versus one of the U*C’s strongest.

1618
01:15:38.100 --> 01:15:40.703
They're finally facing off.

1619
01:15:41.704 --> 01:15:43.539
Incredible. I can't wait to see this.

1620
01:15:44.040 --> 01:15:45.408
It's a battle of the monsters.

1621
01:15:45.474 --> 01:15:48.010
- Wish this had a full three rounds.
- [laughing]

1622
01:15:48.077 --> 01:15:50.679
A battle of the two strongest in Korea.

1623
01:15:51.247 --> 01:15:52.248
Who's your pick?

1624
01:15:52.314 --> 01:15:54.784
- I still say Jung Dawoon.
- I honestly can't pick.

1625
01:15:57.186 --> 01:15:58.988
[Dawoon]
Fans debate about it all the time.

1626
01:15:59.055 --> 01:16:02.658
Who'd win between Myung Hyunman
and Jung Dawoon?

1627
01:16:03.225 --> 01:16:05.261
Honestly, I never gave it much thought.

1628
01:16:05.327 --> 01:16:07.396
I have the same answer for anyone.

1629
01:16:08.130 --> 01:16:09.865
I'm just on another level.

1630
01:16:09.932 --> 01:16:12.601
The difference is astronomical.

1631
01:16:12.668 --> 01:16:15.404
You'd better be ready to give it your all.

1632
01:16:15.471 --> 01:16:19.075
People call me "the old, retired fighter."

1633
01:16:19.141 --> 01:16:22.344
They say I just sell
soy-marinated crabs now.

1634
01:16:22.411 --> 01:16:24.346
But Myung Hyunman is back.

1635
01:16:24.413 --> 01:16:26.715
Dawoon, I'm not the kickboxer
you once knew.

1636
01:16:26.782 --> 01:16:28.818
Now, I'm just a boxer. So brace yourself.

1637
01:16:29.385 --> 01:16:31.287
[Lee] It's the ultimate showdown.

1638
01:16:33.289 --> 01:16:35.091
- Box!
- [bell rings]

1639
01:16:35.157 --> 01:16:36.759
- Box!
- [bell rings]

1640
01:16:36.826 --> 01:16:38.828
- [contestants clamoring]
- Box!

1641
01:16:44.567 --> 01:16:46.068
It's like watching bears fight.

1642
01:16:52.108 --> 01:16:53.375
They're breaking each other.

1643
01:16:54.977 --> 01:16:56.245
That was slick.

1644
01:17:00.049 --> 01:17:01.550
One of them might actually die.

1645
01:17:01.617 --> 01:17:03.085
Those shots look lethal.

1646
01:17:03.152 --> 01:17:04.753
Right there. That can knock you out.

1647
01:17:04.820 --> 01:17:05.955
That hook knocks you out.

1648
01:17:06.021 --> 01:17:07.022
- Right?
- Yeah.

1649
01:17:07.990 --> 01:17:09.125
[contestants exclaim]

1650
01:17:09.925 --> 01:17:12.661
[exclaiming]

1651
01:17:17.133 --> 01:17:18.134
[contestants exclaim]

1652
01:17:20.836 --> 01:17:22.338
- [exclaims]
- [referee] Stop!

1653
01:17:22.404 --> 01:17:23.405
He's down!

1654
01:17:23.839 --> 01:17:24.840
He's down.

1655
01:17:26.375 --> 01:17:28.077
- Whoa, I actually flinched.
- Whoa.

1656
01:17:29.378 --> 01:17:31.580
Whoa! No way!

1657
01:17:35.417 --> 01:17:36.819
[Dawoon] I thought I heard a bomb go off.

1658
01:17:39.121 --> 01:17:40.156
He's terrifying.

1659
01:17:42.358 --> 01:17:45.060
He landed that punch right behind the ear.

1660
01:17:45.561 --> 01:17:47.062
- The temporal region.
- Yeah.

1661
01:17:47.129 --> 01:17:48.130
[contestants exclaiming]

1662
01:17:48.197 --> 01:17:49.265
- [referee] Stop!
- [Lee] He's down!

1663
01:17:49.331 --> 01:17:50.432
That was a heavy hit.

1664
01:17:50.499 --> 01:17:51.667
This could end in a KO.

1665
01:17:53.302 --> 01:17:55.704
- Four, five, six...
- [Dawoon] My vision flashed.

1666
01:17:55.771 --> 01:17:56.772
I was stunned.

1667
01:17:56.839 --> 01:17:58.507
I thought, "This is bad."

1668
01:17:58.574 --> 01:17:59.775
[contestant] Go, Dawoon!

1669
01:18:02.311 --> 01:18:04.146
The look in Dawoon's eyes has changed.

1670
01:18:05.781 --> 01:18:07.483
One of them is going down for sure.

1671
01:18:08.918 --> 01:18:10.853
- Insane!
- Who do you think will win?

1672
01:18:10.920 --> 01:18:12.588
Oh, it's Jang Hyuk!

1673
01:18:13.088 --> 01:18:16.125
[Hyuk]
How far can I make it on my own two feet?

1674
01:18:16.692 --> 01:18:17.693
[contestants exclaim]

1675
01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:19.128
Get in there. Get in there.

1676
01:18:19.595 --> 01:18:21.564
His rhythm's hard to read.

1677
01:18:22.631 --> 01:18:23.966
Do we have bleeding?

1678
01:18:24.033 --> 01:18:25.201
The bleeding won't stop.

1679
01:18:26.101 --> 01:18:27.469
Damn, this place is massive.

1680
01:18:27.536 --> 01:18:29.471
Just how many punching bags are there?

1681
01:18:29.538 --> 01:18:30.806
Round 2 is...

1682
01:18:31.607 --> 01:18:33.042
- a team round.
- Keep going!

1683
01:18:33.108 --> 01:18:35.778
[Lee]
The losing team is immediately eliminated.

1684
01:18:35.844 --> 01:18:37.112
- Let's go, guys!
- Run!

1685
01:18:37.179 --> 01:18:38.380
Last one! Come on!

1686
01:18:38.447 --> 01:18:39.515
- Push through!
- [screams]

1687
01:18:39.582 --> 01:18:41.150
We can win this thing!

1688
01:19:02.404 --> 01:19:04.406
Translated by Jisu Park

